1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:03,101
A psalm's last line and Jesus' last breath

2
00:00:03,161 --> 00:00:06,523
in John close on the very same note: it is

3
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:06,883
done.

4
00:00:07,943 --> 00:00:10,964
The psalm closes looking ahead to God's saving

5
00:00:11,024 --> 00:00:13,825
work, accomplished, and told to a people not

6
00:00:13,865 --> 00:00:14,466
yet born.

7
00:00:15,526 --> 00:00:18,347
Its final line: " that he hath done this."

8
00:00:18,627 --> 00:00:18,927
Done.

9
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:23,829
And as Jesus hung dying, John records His final

10
00:00:23,889 --> 00:00:25,730
word: "It is finished".

11
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:28,411
Different words, in different tongues, a thousand

12
00:00:28,431 --> 00:00:32,593
years apart but the same note: a finished work.

13
00:00:34,073 --> 00:00:35,314
So what's left for you to finish?

14
00:00:36,474 --> 00:00:40,876
Nothing only Someone to come home to: the One

15
00:00:40,936 --> 00:00:42,637
who said it is done.
